            "all": [
              {
                "hasTextMatchesRegex": "\\d{5}"
              },
              {
                "hasNoId": true
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "comment": "#895 (+ the 07-29 F4 field finding): plainMask. The fused 'Apt <n>' unit number is a bounded ~10^4 alphabet over the 4-char length floor, so a 4-hex distinctness suffix is brute-recoverable (the #892/#795 oracle argument); distinctness is redundant here — the same surface's name/street entries keep per-customer hashes. The split label/value form plains via the id-less digit-shape entry below — which only acquired its own `plainMask` in #1039 (round 2): until then this sentence was FALSE on uber, because uber's four copies of that entry were byte-siblings of the doordash ones MINUS the declaration, so the split form hashed a bounded unit number here while the same shape plained on doordash.",
          "find": {
            "hasTextStartsWith": "Apt "
          },
          "keepPrefix": [
            "Apt "
          ],
          "plainMask": true
        },
        {
          "find": {
            "hasTextStartsWith": "\""
          }
        },
        {
          "comment": "#1039 (round 2): plainMask — the byte-sibling of doordash's #889 F1 entry, which has declared it since #889 while these four uber copies did not. The realistic population of this id-less shape is a bare unit number / entry code: a bounded ~10^4 alphabet sitting ABOVE the #889 short-token floor at 4 digits, so the 4-hex distinctness suffix spans 65 536 buckets over 10^4 values and is brute-recoverable (the #892/#795 oracle argument). Distinctness buys nothing here — this surface's name/street entries keep per-customer hashes and a unit number joins nothing. Strictly-stronger mask, capture-only (the node is never parsed), goldens unchanged.",
          "find": {
            "all": [
              {
                "hasTextMatchesRegex": "^#?\\s?\\d{1,4}[A-Za-z]?$"
              },
              {
                "hasNoId": true
              }
